  "notes": [
    "Source: USDA FNS SNAP COLA FY2026 Memo, August 13, 2025. Ronald Ward, Acting Associate Administrator.",
    "Effective October 1, 2025 through September 30, 2026.",
    "Asset limits UNCHANGED from FY2025: $3,000 general, $4,500 elderly/disabled.",
    "Standard deduction for HH sizes 1-3 increased to $209/month (48 states + DC).",
    "Excess shelter cap increased to $744 (48 states + DC).",
    "Homeless shelter deduction increased to $198.99.",
    "The One Big Beautiful Bill Act of 2025 changed certain SNAP work requirements and non-citizen eligibility — check FNS for latest guidance on those provisions.",
    "165% gross income standard applies to elderly/disabled households that are a separate household unit.",
    "Added households_guam, households_virgin_islands, standard_deductions_guam, standard_deductions_virgin_islands, excess_shelter_deduction_cap_guam ($873), and excess_shelter_deduction_cap_virgin_islands ($586) — all transcribed from the same signed FY2026 COLA memo (max allotments p.4, standard deductions and shelter caps p.6). Guam and the U.S. Virgin Islands previously fell back to the 48-states-and-DC tables, which understated their allotments and deductions.",
    "GU and VI intentionally have no households_* gross/net override: the memo's 100%/130%/165% poverty-percentage income tables print one shared column headed '48 States, D.C., Guam, Virgin Islands' (p.3), so households_guam/households_virgin_islands copy gross_monthly/net_monthly from households_48_states_dc verbatim and only max_benefit differs. gross_income_165pct_households_48_states_dc likewise needs no guam/virgin_islands counterpart.",
    "Added minimum_benefit_alaska ($31), minimum_benefit_hawaii ($41), minimum_benefit_guam ($35), and minimum_benefit_virgin_islands ($31) (memo p.5, 1-2 person households). Fixes a pre-existing defect: govsynth previously had only minimum_benefit_48_states_dc and applied that single $24 floor to every region, including Alaska and Hawaii, which have always had higher minimums. Alaska has three allotment tiers (Urban $31 / Rural 1 $39 / Rural 2 $48); minimum_benefit_alaska uses the Urban figure to match the Urban default govsynth already uses for Alaska's max allotment (see max_benefit_urban fallback in govsynth/sources/us/snap.py)."
  ]
